        "Can I trust Easy Tax Refund?",
        "Yes, you can use it with complete peace of mind! I will tell you 3 solid reasons why you can trust Easy Tax Refund. 🛡️\n\n1️⃣ 100% Direct Deposit from the Korean National Tax Service (NTS).\nThis is the part people worry about the most! We never touch your refund money. Once reporting is complete, the refund does not go through us, but the Korean National Tax Service transfers it directly to the account under your name.\n\n2️⃣ Handled by State-Certified Professional Tax Accountants.\nAll refund procedures are legally and meticulously handled by state-certified professional tax accountants of the Republic of Korea with strict qualifications.\n\n3️⃣ Strict Personal Information Protection\nIdentity verification and personal information are used solely for the purpose of reporting tax refunds to the government (NTS) system, and are safely protected under strict security.\n\nEvery year, we are safely finding 'the money you should rightfully get back' that many foreign workers are missing out on because they don't know. Relax and start checking according to the on-screen instructions! 👍",
        "Why do I have to pay a fee?",
        "The 25% fee is a rightful service fee (labor cost) for the 'Professional Tax Accountant' who will meticulously recalculate your taxes and report them to the NTS on your behalf. 👨‍💼💼\n\nA tax refund is not something where money just comes out by pressing a button, but rather a complex legal procedure where a tax accountant must personally analyze the complex tax records of the past 5 years and submit reporting documents to the NTS.\n\n⚠️ The real reason you have to pay the fee in advance!\nYour refund does not go through us but is 100% directly deposited from the 'Korean National Tax Service' to 'Your Account'. Therefore, it is absolutely impossible for our system to deduct the fee from your refund and transfer it to you.\n(However, if the tax accountant's final review determines that a refund is impossible, the fee you paid will be 100% refunded immediately!)",
        "When will it be deposited?",
        "After completing the refund application, it usually takes about 45 days to a maximum of 60 days for the money to be deposited into your actual bank account. ⏳\n\nThe reason it takes quite some time is because the officials of the Korean National Tax Service (NTS) require a review period to carefully check and approve your tax records for the past 5 years one by one. (It may be slightly faster or slower depending on the workload of the local tax office.)\n\nYou can always check the progress of the refund in real-time in Easy Tax Refund's [My Refund Status] menu, so please wait with peace of mind!",
        "Is my ID photo safe?",
        "Yes, it is 100% safe! I fully understand your concern that your ID photo might be used in a bad place. We promise 3 strict security principles of Easy Tax Refund. 🔒\n\n1️⃣ Permanently Deleted Immediately Upon Sending (NO Saving!)\nThe ID photo you take is never 'saved' on our servers or mobile phones. It is permanently destroyed immediately after it is submitted to the tax office solely for the purpose of identity verification.\n\n2️⃣ Mandatory Document Required by the NTS (Government)\nIn order for the Korean National Tax Service (NTS) to approve a tax refund, they strictly require a copy of an ID to verify 'whether this person is really who they say they are'. We merely play the role of submitting this mandatory document to the NTS on your behalf, and it can never be used for any other purposes such as getting a loan or opening a mobile phone.\n\n3️⃣ Bank-Level Encryption Security\nAll your information is transmitted directly to the NTS through a powerful encryption system at the same level as major banks in Korea.\n\nYour valuable personal information will never be leaked, so please take a picture of your ID according to the instructions with peace of mind!",
        "Why does the inquiry result show a refund amount of 0 won?",
        "Did your inquiry result show a refund amount of 0 won? This may be a normal result. 📊\n\nA tax refund is getting back 'the tax you are entitled to get back' from 'the taxes you have paid'. If your previous company handled the year-end tax settlement perfectly, or if the tax you paid was already small, there might be no additional amount (hidden tax) to get back.\n\nEven though the refund amount is 0 won this time, you may have a refund if you inquire again next year or after changing jobs, so be sure to visit Easy Tax Refund again next year!",
        "Can I receive it in a bank account under someone else's name?",
